&lt;h1 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director of Paid Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing · Full-time · Remote (US) · Core hours 9-5 EST&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nysonian&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nysonian is a $250 million dollar consumer products company built around two brands: &lt;a href=&quot;https://nobltravel.com/&quot;&gt;NOBL&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://pilatesflo.com/&quot;&gt;Flo Pilates&lt;/a&gt;. We grew revenue 8x in 2025 and are building the next phase of the US-based business across physical products, software, and subscription experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NOBL is a functional travel brand built around a simple idea: travel products should solve real problems, not just look better. Every feature is designed to eliminate friction from the travel experience — from seamless organization and easy access, to tracking, connectivity, and protection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flo Pilates brings studio-quality Pilates into the home through connected fitness hardware, content, and subscription experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across both brands, we&#39;re building product ecosystems that deepen the customer relationship beyond the initial purchase and create recurring value over time. We&#39;re looking for builders who want autonomy, speed, and the ability to shape products at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nysonian is hiring a Head of Paid Media to own acquisition performance across NOBL and Flo, personally managing paid channels at scale and driving profitable growth. This role reports to Daniel (Co-CEO) and works closely with the performance creative and data teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on media buying across Meta, Google, TikTok, Snapchat, and AppLovin; Launching campaigns, analyzing performance, and making spending decisions daily across all brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Landing-page creation and testing: turning campaign insights into page variants tailored to specific ads, audiences, and offers. You&#39;ll execute this yourself, not request it from others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep account analysis: connecting ad performance to landing-page behavior, conversion data, and funnel dynamics to diagnose what&#39;s working and what&#39;s broken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hypothesis development and testing: forming your own theories about platform dynamics and account optimization, then running live tests to validate them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling strategy and execution: determining how much incremental spend each channel and campaign can absorb, where to redirect budget, and when to cut or consolidate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance monitoring and autonomous decision-making seven days a week. Accounts need attention on weekends, and you won&#39;t hand off buying responsibility because it&#39;s Saturday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent, hands-on media-buying experience: you personally launched, analyzed, and scaled campaigns in Meta Ads Manager. A management title or big brand on your résumé doesn&#39;t count—we need evidence you did the actual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally managed at least $1 million per month in media spend that you controlled directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct-response copywriting and landing-page creation: you&#39;ve written hooks, offers, objections, and proof points, and built and tested landing-page variations yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Meta knowledge and obsessive attention to platform dynamics, including original thinking about campaign structure, targeting, and scaling approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical foundation: you understand CAC, new-customer ROAS, attribution limits, and how to move beyond &quot;ROAS is down&quot; to diagnose root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect acquisition performance to creative, offers, funnels, and landing pages—you see the full customer journey, not just ad-account metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI workflow already in active use: you have a demonstrated, concrete workflow showing how AI helps you analyze, write, build, or test faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with autonomy and influence: you propose the next move, don&#39;t wait for us to decide it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Is Not a Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve never personally created and tested landing pages yourself, or you treat landing-page, copy, and offer improvements as someone else&#39;s responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You stop analyzing at &quot;ROAS is down&quot; and can&#39;t dig through the ad, page, and conversion process to identify the likely problem and recommend a specific change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You wait for direction on what to test or where to adjust spending instead of proposing priorities yourself and expecting to execute on your own call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You won&#39;t personally manage the accounts on weekends or you view this as a nine-to-five role where account coverage ends Friday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use a market-based approach to compensation. The expected total compensation range for this role is: USD $200,000 to $250,000. This role also offers a performance-based bonus tied to business impact (OTE $300-350k).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working at Nysonian&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Culture&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We&#39;re founder-led and operate with speed, direct communication, and clear accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We invest in tools and management practices that help colleagues do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our products are used by customers globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI is intentionally embedded in how we work, create, and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior leaders are expected to create structure, make decisions, and stay close to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Development&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pay and meaningful opportunities for performance-based advancement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of strategy, systems, execution, and team buildout within your function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to build and scale a meaningful part of the business across two consumer brands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and compensation growth tied to performance, role expansion, and measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance options for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% Paid for Life and Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nine (9) paid holidays per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary NOBL &amp;amp; Flo Pilates products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first — core operating hours are 9-5 EST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, sex, religion, gender, marital status, natio&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;nal origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status or other characteristics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
